A sequence of messages \( m_1, \ldots, mk \) is suitable if for every \( 1 \leq j \leq k \), 
- (i) \( m_j \) is of the form \( (m_0^j, m_1^j) \), where both \( m_0^j \) and \( m_1^j \) are either identical creation queries or messages of the forms \( (q_0, \ell) \) and \( (q_1, \ell) \) with the same index \( \ell \); 
- (ii) for each \( b \in \{0, 1\} \), if \( m_b^j = (q, \ell) \), then the sequences formed by the first messages of all message pairs and the sequence formed by the second messages of all message pairs are neighboring.
